@startuml

' The end-to-end flow that turns a folder of images into reviewable duplicate groups
' Three GPU signals are computed (ZNCC similarity, Laplacian sharpness, perceptual hash);
' the clustering and keeper selection then run on the CPU over the resulting matrices/scores

title ImgLabs — Duplicate Detection Pipeline

skinparam shadowing false

start
:Import images;
:Resample to a common canvas\n(smaller of the set minimum or the Max Canvas Size cap);
:Grayscale every image once\n(shared full-canvas batch — ImageAnalysisSession);
note right
  Computed a single time and reused by
  both the ZNCC matrix and the sharpness score
end note

fork
  :Build the ZNCC similarity matrix\n(all pairs, lower triangle only — ZNCC is symmetric);
  note right
    Each pair scored on the GPU:
    grayscale -> mean -> subtract-mean ->
    square -> sum -> dot product
  end note
fork again
  :Score Laplacian sharpness per image\n(3x3 Laplacian convolution -> variance of the result);
fork again
  :Perceptual hash per image\n(own 32x32 grayscale -> DCT -> 8x8 low-freq -> median -> 64-bit);
  :Build the all-pairs Hamming-distance matrix;
end fork

:Cluster with Union-Find\n(connect a pair when ZNCC >= threshold OR Hamming <= tolerance);
:Choose one keeper per cluster\n(WeightedQualityStrategy: sharpness + resolution +\nfile size + format + representativeness; medoid fallback);
:Render duplicate groups\n(DuplicateView, keep vs. remove);
:Export keepers to a folder\n(cluster keepers + images in no cluster);
stop

@enduml
